<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI3152-REGISTRY-PUSHDISPATCH-UNBOUNDED-JOIN>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI3152-REGISTRY-PUSHDISPATCH-UNBOUNDED-JOIN" ;
  triage:title "Unbounded join_handle.join() in active_connection_registry.rs push_dispatch_handle error paths" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr's M5-ADMISSION-POSTMERGE-REVIEWERBACKED review (task #1417) surfaced this NEW, out-of-scope finding on integrate/phase-ai-31-33: crates/atm-daemon/src/active_connection_registry.rs:131 and :136, inside push_dispatch_handle's error paths, call join_handle.join() without timeout/deadline bound. This is the same unbounded-join-at-shutdown defect class as the 6 findings just fixed in M5-ADMISSION-FIX-4/POSTMERGE, which established the pattern of bounding joins with a shared completion-channel timeout primitive. Notably, this same file already has the bounded join_dispatch_handle_with_timeout primitive (TRACKED_DISPATCH_JOIN_DEADLINE, 250ms) used elsewhere; these two error-path call sites appear to bypass it." ;
